{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789404836,"nonce":"Y2QXv7jbB653kE09XlktituzNyg=","message":"2026-09-14, the scheduler: 7776341 (src/runtime/sched.rs). Not M:N —\none world per VM on the thread that owns it, as the plan says; M:N is\n6b20a51 and sits on top of this. Shape mirrors caribou's sched: tasks\nmap + ready queue + timer min-heap, a global wait registry with\nclaim-then-deliver (a wake marks Notified and mails the world; a due\ntimer claims only a still-Waiting token; both remove the entry), an\nendpoint per world (mutex queue + condvar) so a wake from any thread\nlands, and the driver idles on the condvar until a wake, a timer or\nits deadline.\n\nWren surface, all Fiber statics (a new core class name would collide\nwith hatch-events' Scheduler): spawn(fn) -\u003e Fiber, sleep(ms), waiter\n-\u003e token, park(token, ms) -\u003e Bool, wake(token) -\u003e Bool, tick(ms) -\u003e\nBool (live tasks remain), idle(ms), live. A task's abort ends it and\nstays in fiber.error, as under try. tick/idle from a task is an error.\nA park from under a task on a fiber the task called travels up:\ntry_krio_call re-yields the intermediate while the world holds a\npending park and re-enters the callee on resume.\n\nNeeds stacks: WLIFT_KRIO_FIBER=0 leaves the natives erroring; the\nwasm target binds stubs. Task fibers are GC roots via VM.sched.\n\nVerified: lib/e2e/krio/hatch_runner on default and llvm features, e2e\nunder WLIFT_GC_STRESS=1 and WLIFT_KRIO_FIBER=0, aot_runtime (23) +\naot_gc_coverage, wasm_smoke, the tiered corpus 42/42 (plain and\n--jit-threshold 1 --opt-threshold 4 under GC stress), the AOT corpus\n42/42, hatch/site tiered and AOT plain and stressed; NUC numbers\nunchanged (fib 0.42 s, method_call 0.09, binary_trees 0.57, nbody\n1.05, generator 0.30).\n\nLeft on this issue: the epoch-word poll at compiled loop headers\n(only a timer-driven scheduler or a cross-thread GC stop needs it),\nand moving hatch-web's Scheduler_/Clock.sleepMs(1) loop onto\nspawn/tick(0)/idle(1) — hatch's call.","files":null}]}